# Adapter: @apply only, no inline styles

- Markup (templ and Svelte) carries only semantic classes: `ui-*` (packages, defined in `packages/adapter/src/*.css`) and `ds-*` (apps/design-svelte docs shell, `apps/design-svelte/src/lib/styles/*.css`). Never Tailwind utilities in markup, never `style="…"`, never `style:` directives.
- Every utility lives in an `@apply` rule: `.ui-stats-row-list { @apply grid grid-cols-2 gap-6 md:grid-cols-4; }`.
- Tailwind is imported with `source(none)` — no content scanning, so a utility in markup would silently not exist.
- Primitive classes come from `packages/ui/recipes/*.variants.json` (generator rewrites them to `ui-*`); block classes from the `css:` field in `packages/blocks/defs`. Do not edit `*.generated.css`.
- Per-value visual samples (swatches, sizes) get one generated class each (`packages/design-docs/scripts/foundations.ts`), not inline styles.
